Question 10 - Symbol Reference

    <h3>1. Reserved Characters</h3>

    <p>
        HTML uses &lt; and &gt; for tags, while &amp; represents
        the ampersand character.
    </p>


    <h3>2. Currency Symbols</h3>

    <p>
        Common currencies include &euro; Euro,
        &pound; Pound and &yen; Yen.
    </p>


    <h3>3. Mathematical Symbols</h3>

    <p>
        Examples include &ne; for not equal,
        &#x2211; for summation and &#8734; for infinity.
    </p>


    <h3>4. Arrows</h3>

    <p>
        Navigation arrows include &larr; Back,
        &#x2192; Next and &#8593; Top.
    </p>


    <h3>5. Emojis And Legal Symbols</h3>

    <p>
        &#x1F600; represents a smiling face,
        &copy; represents copyright and
        &reg; represents a registered trademark.
    </p>


